text:
maya: Heads-up — I'm starting a small rollout for header-based feature flags in the JS SDK. Need quick sync on guardrails: header format, canary audience, and how we handle older SDKs.

juan: 👍 what header name are we thinking? x-rw-feature? x-redwood-flags?

li: prefer short: `x-rw-flags`. payload as semicolon kv pairs, e.g. `feature_x=on;feature_y=off;ver=2` so parsers are simple.

priya: important: SDK should ignore unknown keys to keep forward-compat. older SDKs (<=2.0.3) might not parse — we need a fallback plan.

tom: for canary scope, let's do org-level first (org_id hash mod 100 < pct) then user-level. server will only send header when request falls into canary. avoids SDK complexity.

juan: agree. server-side rollout + header injection is clean. also add a min-sdk-version attribute so server only injects header when SDK >= 2.1.0. otherwise server uses legacy gating.

li: quick code sample for JS SDK parsing (proposal):
```js
// in transport layer
const header = response.headers.get('x-rw-flags');
if (header) {
  header.split(';').forEach(pair => {
    const [k, v] = pair.split('=');
    if (k) flags[k] = v === 'on' ? true : v === 'off' ? false : v;
  });
}
// SDK consumers check flags.feature_x before enabling new behaviour
```

maya: nice. can we ensure parsing is O(n) and very defensive (try/catch) so malformed headers don't blow up requests?

li: yep, we'll wrap parse in try/catch and fallback to empty flags on error.

priya: QA ask: how do we test older SDKs? we should add an integration test matrix: sdk_version x server_inject_header boolean -> expected behaviour. I'll add to the QA board.

tom: operator guardrails: server should rate-limit header injection changes and log rollout events to metrics (percent, orgs, time window). also expose a rollback toggle.

juan: operational note: add a lint rule in the SDK to warn when code reads flags without a default (so devs don't assume flag=true). small checklist item for the PR.

deploy-bot: deploy scheduled to canary infra at 2025-06-12T15:30Z (job 7890).

maya: next steps:
- li to implement parsing + defensive tests (PR)
- juan to add server injection rule + min-sdk-version logic (ticket created)
- priya to add regression matrix tests
- tom to add metrics/rollback hooks

maya: I'll run a tiny canary (5 orgs) for 48h then ramp to 25% if no regressions. tagging @everyone involved. :rocket:

sasha-bot: note: created ticket RW-1428 for server-side injection and RW-1429 for SDK parsing.

maya: thanks all — ping me in thread for any blockers.
